    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d316">

                <pb facs="0520" n="434" sameAs="frus:frus1927v01/pg434"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">835.34/428: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Cable</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-08-18T14:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 18,
                                1927—2 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>31. Embassy’s telegram No. 70, dated August 9, 5 p.m. You are instructed to
                    request an audience with the President and tell him that the Department, with a
                    desire to insure full and careful consideration of the Electric Boat Company’s
                    proposition, sincerely hopes that no decision will be made until the company has
                    had the opportunity to present evidence of the arrangements made by it in France
                    on the understanding that the matter had been decided virtually in the company’s
                        favor.<anchor n="10" xml:id="d316-f1"/></p>
                <p>The delay is partly desired in order that the Electric Boat Company may have time
                    to enlist the support of the Government of France. Because of President Alvear’s
                    well-known disposition to favor France, the company believes this may be
                    effective.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d316-f1" n="10" xml:id="d316-f1-content">
                <p>In a letter of Aug. 20, 1927, the Electric Boat Co. informed the Department that
                    the Government of Argentina had agreed to postpone the final decision; letter
                    not printed. (File No. 835.34/435.)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
